id: SCA-071
title: PATH manipulation to shadow system binaries
category: supply-chain
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .sh .bash
  filenames: Makefile .bashrc .zshrc .profile
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: export\s+PATH\s*=\s*[^$]*:\$PATH
    message: Prepending directory to PATH can shadow system binaries (git, node, etc.), causing subsequent commands to execute attacker version.
  - regex: PATH=.*:\$PATH.*export
    message: PATH modification prepends untrusted directory — may shadow system binaries with malicious versions.
fix: Audit all PATH modifications. Ensure prepended directories are trusted and not world-writable. Use absolute paths for security-critical commands.
